@startuml
layout compact
package services::opc::model {
  class Fan
  class TripOrder
  class Payment
  class Attendee
  class SupplierOrder
  abstract class TripItem
  class FestivalPass
  class LodgingStay
  class Experience
  abstract class TransportItem
  class ShuttleRide
}
TripOrder "0..*" --> "1" Fan : buyer
TripOrder "1" *-- "1" Payment : payment
TripOrder "1" *-- "1..8" Attendee : attendees
TripOrder "1" *-- "1..*" TripItem : items
TripOrder "1" *-- "0..*" SupplierOrder : supplier_orders
TripItem "1..*" --> "1..*" Attendee : attendees
SupplierOrder "0..1" --> "0..*" TripItem : items
FestivalPass --|> TripItem
LodgingStay --|> TripItem
Experience --|> TripItem
TransportItem --|> TripItem
ShuttleRide --|> TransportItem
note top of TripOrder
Multiplicities from type hints and
validators: one payment
(services/opc/model/orders.py:50),
1 to 8 attendees
(services/opc/model/orders.py:57),
at least one item
(services/opc/model/orders.py:59).
end note
note right of SupplierOrder
One trip order per supplier order
(services/opc/model/suppliers.py:21).
end note
note bottom of Experience
{every attendee of an Experience holds
a FestivalPass on the same order}
(services/opc/model/rules.py:22)
end note
note left of TripItem
{the attendees of an item are attendees of its
trip order} (services/opc/model/rules.py:14)
Each item has at least one attendee
(services/opc/model/items.py:24).
end note
note left of Fan
Key: UML 2.5.1 class diagram.
Filled diamond: composition; the trip
order owns the part.
Arrow: navigable association, named
after the field.
Hollow triangle: generalization.
Italic name, {abstract}: abstract class.
{…} in a note: a constraint the
code enforces.
end note
@layout
Fan @pos(426, 0)
Attendee @pos(160, 220)
TripOrder @pos(420, 220)
Payment @pos(740, 220)
TripItem @pos(400, 470)
SupplierOrder @pos(760, 482)
FestivalPass @pos(40, 760)
LodgingStay @pos(280, 760)
Experience @pos(520, 760)
TransportItem @pos(800, 760)
ShuttleRide @pos(811, 970)
note:45 @pos(32, 528)
@endlayout
@enduml
